s($,"aTd","X9",()=>A.a([A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.H7),"Ramesh Kumar","1","Saved 12 families (47 people) from a building fire. The local community raised funds for his medical treatment and children's education.",!0,1247,"Mumbai, India","Security Guard","For 15 years, Ramesh has been the night security guard at a residential complex. One night, he noticed smoke coming from a third-floor apartment. Without hesitation, he ran up, banged on doors, and helped evacuate 12 families before the fire spread. He suffered minor burns but saved everyone.","The Midnight Guardian"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.Ha),"Priya Sharma","2","Educated over 200 children. 15 of her students have now completed high school, and 3 are in college.",!0,2156,"Delhi, India","Teacher","Priya noticed that children of migrant workers living under a bridge had no access to education. Every evening after her school job, she would come to the bridge with a small blackboard and teach them for free. She's been doing this for 8 years now.","Teaching Under the Bridge"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.Hf),"Mary Johnson","3","Donated 10,000+ items to shelters. Started a 'Second Chance' program now adopted by the city.",!1,892,"New York, USA","Sanitation Worker","Mary has been a sanitation worker for 20 years. During her routes, she started noticing discarded items that were still usable. She began collecting them, cleaning them up, and donating them to homeless shelters. She's donated over 10,000 items.","The Garbage Angel"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.Hh),"Sarah Chen","4","Cared for 500+ COVID patients. Facilitated over 100 family video calls during final moments.",!0,3421,"Seattle, USA","Nurse","During COVID-19, Sarah worked 16-hour shifts for months. She would video call families of dying patients so they could say goodbye. She held the hands of those who had no one. She contracted COVID twice but returned to work both times after recovery.","Nurse During the Pandemic"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.GV),"Gurpreet Singh","5","Fed over 5,000 people during lockdown. Inspired 20 other farmers to join his initiative.",!1,1876,"Punjab, India","Farmer","Despite facing his own financial difficulties, Gurpreet donates 10% of his harvest every year to a local food bank. During the lockdown, he drove his tractor 50 km to deliver free vegetables to stranded migrant workers.","The Farmer Who Feeds Thousands"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.Hg),"Ahmed Hassan","6","Made over 500 free deliveries to elderly citizens. Other delivery workers have now joined his cause.",!1,756,"Cairo, Egypt","Delivery Worker","Ahmed noticed that many elderly customers couldn't afford delivery fees. He started a personal initiative - every 10th delivery he makes, he uses his own money to deliver groceries free to an elderly person in need. He's done this for 3 years.","Delivering Hope"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.GX),"Michael O'Brien","7","Started 'Toys from Ashes' program. Donated toys to 10,000+ children across 15 states.",!0,2543,"Boston, USA","Firefighter","After rescuing a 5-year-old boy from a house fire, Michael learned the boy lost all his toys. He organized the fire department to collect toys for children affected by fires. The program has now spread to 15 states.","The Firefighter's Promise"),A.oA(A.o5().hF(B.H1),"Rosa Martinez","8","Brought smiles to thousands of sick children. Hospital officially recognized her with a 'Heart of Gold' award.",!1,1654,"Los Angeles, USA","Hospital Janitor","Rosa works as a janitor in a children's hospital. She noticed lonely children and started bringing small toys and drawing pictures for them during her breaks. The children call her 'Mama Rosa'. She's been doing this for 12 years.","Cleaning with Compassion")],A.aH("B<id>")))
